mixin () {
  /// Static behavioral API documentation for AI assistants reading this canister
  /// through the ICP MCP connector. Authored from source; reads no runtime state.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Marginalia Backend API\n\nMarginalia is a formative-assessment app for teachers and students. A teacher authors an assignment with a concept graph; a student writes an answer, gets per-concept Socratic feedback from an LLM, revises across saved versions, and submits the work. This document describes the canister's public Candid API for an AI assistant calling it through the ICP MCP connector.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nSign-in uses Internet Identity. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nEvery method that reads or writes user data requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. Anonymous callers receive a trap on guarded endpoints.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\nA direct API caller must register before any role-guarded call:\n\n1. Call `registerProfile(role, name)` once as a signed-in caller. `role` is `#teacher` or `#student`. This creates the caller's profile and a pending approval request, and mirrors the role into the authorization extension (teachers become admins).\n2. The first caller to initialize access control through the frontend's sign-in flow receives the admin role; subsequent callers receive the user role. A teacher account is an admin and is auto-approved.\n3. Until an admin calls `decideApproval(user, #approved)`, the account is pending. `getAccessStatus()` reports `registered`, `approved`, `role`, and `name`.\n\nAn unregistered caller calling a guarded endpoint receives a trap such as `notAuthorized: sign-in required to ...` or `notFound: no profile registered for caller`. An anonymous caller receives `notAuthorized: sign-in required to ...`.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Timestamps** are nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, signed `Int` (`Time.now()`). Convert to milliseconds by dividing by 1,000,000 for display.\n- **Identifiers** (`Id`) are `Nat`, allocated from a single monotonic counter shared across all entities.\n- **Principals** are the caller identity; every owner/author field is a `Principal`.\n- **Optional values** are Candid `opt`; `null` means absent.\n- **Variants**: `AppRole` = `#teacher | #student`; `ApprovalState` = `#pending | #approved | #rejected`; `ConceptStatus` = `#covered | #partial | #missing | #misconception`; `OverrideStatus` = `#none | #accepted | #overridden`; `SubmissionStatus` = `#draft | #submitted`; `MarginNoteType` = `#question | #highlight | #summary`.\n- **Coverage** is a percentage `Float` in `[0, 100]`, weighted by concept weight (`covered` counts fully, `partial` half, everything else zero).\n- **Confidence** is a `Float` in `[0, 1]`.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### Identity\n\n- `registerProfile(role : AppRole, name : Text) : async ()` — signed-in only; traps if the caller already registered.\n- `getMyProfile() : async ?ProfileView` — the caller's profile, or `null`.\n- `updateProfileName(name : Text) : async ()` — traps if the caller has no profile.\n- `getAccessStatus() : async AccessStatus` — registration/approval/role status; safe to poll after sign-in.\n- `listApprovalRequests() : async [ApprovalRequestView]` — admin only; traps otherwise.\n- `decideApproval(user : Principal, decision : ApprovalState) : async ()` — admin only; traps if no request exists for `user`.\n\n### Assignments and concepts (teacher)\n\n- `createAssignment(title, prompt, rubricText) : async Id` — signed-in only.\n- `listTeacherAssignments() : async [AssignmentView]` — the caller's own assignments.\n- `getAssignment(assignment : Id) : async ?AssignmentView` — `null` when the caller may not read it.\n- `addConcept(assignment, name, description, weight, misconception) : async Id` — only the assignment's teacher; traps otherwise.\n- `listConcepts(assignment : Id) : async [ConceptView]` — empty when the caller may not read the assignment.\n\n### Student submissions and feedback\n\n- `listAssignedTasks() : async [AssignedTask]` — the caller student's tasks, each with its latest coverage.\n- `getOrCreateSubmission(assignment : Id) : async SubmissionView` — idempotent; returns the existing submission or creates a `#draft`. Traps if the caller is the assignment's teacher.\n- `getFeedback(submission : Id, text : Text) : async FeedbackResult` — runs the LLM concept-graph evaluation and persists a new version with per-concept results. Only the submission's student may call it. On model failure it traps with `llmFailed: ...`; the frontend shows an error toast. Each `evidenceQuote` is an exact substring of `text` or `null`; each `nudge` is a Socratic question that never reveals the answer.\n- `listVersions(submission : Id) : async [VersionView]` — oldest first.\n- `getVersion(version : Id) : async ?VersionView` — `null` when the caller may not read it.\n- `listConceptResults(version : Id) : async [ConceptResultView]` — empty when the caller may not read the version.\n- `getGrowthTimeline(submission : Id) : async GrowthTimeline` — coverage points across versions plus a before/after concept diff and `fixedCount`.\n- `submitToTeacher(submission : Id) : async ()` — only the student; sets status `#submitted`.\n- `overrideConceptResult(result : Id, status : OverrideStatus, comment : ?Text) : async ()` — only the assignment's teacher; records a teacher override of one AI judgement.\n- `listAssignmentSubmissions(assignment : Id) : async [SubmissionView]` — only the assignment's teacher; empty otherwise.\n\n### Reading Mode\n\n- `createReading(title, content) : async Id` — signed-in only.\n- `listReadings() : async [ReadingView]` — the caller's own readings.\n- `getReading(reading : Id) : async ?ReadingView` — `null` when the caller does not own it.\n- `addMarginNote(reading, noteType, anchorText, question) : async Id` — only the reading's owner.\n- `listMarginNotes(reading : Id) : async [MarginNoteView]` — empty when the caller does not own the reading.\n- `answerMarginNote(note : Id, response : Text) : async ()` — only the reading's owner.\n- `saveReadingEvaluation(reading, scoresJson, feedbackJson) : async Id` — only the reading's owner.\n- `listReadingEvaluations(reading : Id) : async [ReadingEvaluationView]` — empty when the caller does not own the reading.\n\n## Authorization boundaries\n\n- Students see only their own submissions, versions, concept results, readings, margin notes, and evaluations.\n- Teachers see only their own assignments and the submissions to those assignments.\n- Admin-only methods (`listApprovalRequests`, `decideApproval`) trap for non-admins.\n- Read methods that the caller may not access return `null` or an empty array rather than trapping.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- After sign-in, poll `getAccessStatus()` until `registered` is true, then until `approved` is true. A pending account cannot use the app.\n- A submission starts `#draft`. Each `getFeedback` call appends a new version; `submitToTeacher` moves it to `#submitted`.\n- `getFeedback` is a long-running update call (it performs an HTTPS outcall). Show a skeleton loader while it is in flight.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `getOrCreateSubmission` is idempotent: retrying returns the same submission.\n- `getFeedback` is **not** idempotent: each successful call persists a new version and consumes inference. Do not auto-retry; retry only on explicit user action.\n- `registerProfile` traps on a second call for the same caller; treat that trap as \"already registered\".\n- `createAssignment`, `addConcept`, `createReading`, `addMarginNote`, and `saveReadingEvaluation` each allocate a new id per call; retrying creates a duplicate row.\n- `submitToTeacher`, `overrideConceptResult`, `updateProfileName`, `answerMarginNote`, and `decideApproval` are idempotent in effect.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Traps are opaque rejects. Common messages: `notAuthorized: ...`, `notFound: ...`, `invalidInput: ...`, `llmFailed: ...`.\n- `getFeedback` traps with `llmFailed: ...` when the model is unreachable or returns an unreadable response; the frontend surfaces this as a friendly toast.\n- The LLM never reveals the correct answer; nudges are guiding questions only.\n- Every AI judgement carries a `confidence` and is teacher-overridable via `overrideConceptResult`.\n- `listApprovalRequests` and `decideApproval` require an admin (teacher) caller.\n";
  };
};
